card.statement:
Let $A$ be an algebra in the category $\cC(\h,\Omega)$ with a non-degenerate multiplicative bilinear form and with the trivial subalgebra of invariants $A^\h=k$. Then $\gl=\gl(A)$ is a subgroup of $\h$ and $A$ is isomorphic to a skew group algebra $k[\gl,\alpha]$ for some 2-cocycle $\alpha:\gl\times\gl\to k^\cro$, i.e.
$A$ is spanned by $e_x, x\in\gl$ with multiplication

\begin{equation}
e_xe_y = \alpha(x,y)e_{x+y}.
\end{equation}

\newline
The $\h$-action has a form:

\begin{equation}
y(e_x) = (x,y)e_x,\quad \forall x\in\gl, y\in\h.
\end{equation}
